.\" Man page for opip
.\" vim: ft=man
.TH OPIP 1 "2026-06-14" "1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
opip \- Create and install integrity-backed offline Python wheel bundles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opip
[\fB--data-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB--no-color\fR]
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Build, verify, and install offline Python wheel bundles (\.opip) for
sneakernet and air-gapped targets. Bundles include integrity manifests,
lock files, SBOM metadata, and optional Reticulum RSG signatures.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS create
Fetch wheels from PyPI and pack them into a bundle.
.B opip create
[\fB-o\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB-C\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB-r\fR \fIREQ.txt\fR]
[\fB--python\fR \fIVERSION\fR] [\fB--platform\fR \fITAG\fR]
[\fB--publisher\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB--identity\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fIpackages\fR...]
.SS install
Install a bundle from a local file, rns:// remote, URL, or git source.
.B opip install
\fISOURCE\fR
[\fB--signer\fR \fIIDENTITY\fR] [\fB--require-signature\fR]
[\fB--user\fR] [\fB--replace\fR]
.SS verify
Verify bundle integrity, authenticity, and provenance.
.SS export
Copy a verified bundle for offline sharing (includes .rsg sidecar when present).
.SS list
List registered bundles or installed bundle records.
.SS uninstall
Uninstall packages installed from a registered bundle.
.SS update
Rebuild a registered bundle from stored requirements.
.SS keygen
Generate a Reticulum identity for bundle signing.
.SS register-windows
Register .opip file association and Explorer context menus (Windows).
.SH EXAMPLES
.B Bundle a project:
.RS
opip create
.RE
.B Install on an air-gapped machine:
.RS
opip verify my-bundle.opip
.br
opip install my-bundle.opip
.RE
.B Install from Reticulum:
.RS
opip install rns://identity/group/repo@v1.0.0
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPIP_DATA_DIR
State directory for bundle registry and install records.
.TP
.B OPIP_SIGNER
Default signer identity for verify and install.
.TP
.B PIP_RNS_CONFIG
Config directory for pip-rns aliases resolved during rns:// installs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pip-rns (1),
.BR pipx-rns (1)
